ountability structures. If a risk is truly uninsurable, it should not be hidden behind proprietary opacity; it must be exposed to the market through mandated open-access research pathways that force developers to internalize the cost of their architecture. When we require that AI developers publish their training methodologies and safety evaluation protocols, we invite a global network of researchers to identify vulnerabilities that a single, closed-source team would miss. This transition from proprietary gatekeeping to a transparent, competitive oversight market is the only viable way to manage the development of systems that may soon exceed our individual cognitive capacity.",
